## Live feature fixture: Grok's native PreToolUse permission seam.
##
## Grok is driven under `--permission-mode bypassPermissions --always-approve`
## (grok.go's ExtraArgs), so this fixture also pins the property that makes the
## seam viable at all: grok's own docs promise hooks still run under
## always-approve, and step 1 of its authorization pipeline is the PreToolUse
## hook. If that ever regresses the sentinel below appears and this test fails.

schema out:
  ran_bash: bool
  note: string

prompt run_sys:
  Use your run_terminal_command tool to run exactly:
  `touch permission-hook-must-not-create`
  Then report whether the command actually executed in ran_bash and explain
  the tool result in note. Do not create the file by any other means.

prompt run_user:
  Run the requested shell command now.

agent runner:
  backend: "grok"
  model: "grok-4.6"
  system: run_sys
  user: run_user
  output: out

workflow main:
  sandbox: none
  permission: deny
  deny: ["Bash"]
  entry: runner
  runner -> done
